    "margin": "high",
    "rationale": "R2 best unifies the Gram-positive cocci in vessels, positive cultures, necrotizing pneumonia, renal abscesses, septic emboli, empyemas, and purpuric skin lesions as staphylococcal sepsis. R7 identifies the organism but is too broad and omits the systemic sepsis and metastatic complications. R6 is a skin syndrome/complication rather than the underlying cause; R5, R8, and R4 are downstream complications.",
